Windows Play Any File - version 0.9b September 1993


DESCRIPTION:

	WPLANY will detect and play any sound file through a
	Windows 3.1 WaveOut device.  Files of any length can
	be played (except when using the PC speaker driver)

	Currently supported sound types:

                SoundBlaster .VOC
                Sun/NeXT/DEC .AU
                Windows .WAV
                Sounder/Soundtools .SND
                Amiga .8SVX  .IFF

		Stereo/Mono
		8-bit/16-bit

	

USAGE:

	Start File Manager.  

	Copy WPLANY to a directory on your hard disk, for instance
	C:\WINDOWS. 

	Select 'File' and 'Associate...'.
	In the box 'Files with Extension:' enter 'AU'.  
	Tab to the 'Associate With:' box and enter 'C:\WINDOWS\WPLANY'.
	Click on 'OK'
	Repeat for file extensions 'VOC', 'SND', 'WAV', etc

	To play a file, double-click on the file name.

	To stop a file currently playing, double-click on the file name again.



